From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: a hook on another process's thread only within the hooker's desktop, session and user

set_hook found a hook's target thread by its id anywhere in the server and checked only UIPI
(no hooking an elevated program from below). In a prefix several Unix users share, one user
could hook another user's programs: an in-context hook loads the hooker's module into the
other user's thread, and since 8403 an out-of-context WinEvent hook brings that thread's
window events (creation, focus, moves, with window handles) back without any module. Windows
keeps hooks to one desktop, and each logon has its own.

A hook on a thread of another process -- in context or out of context -- now needs that
thread on the hooker's own desktop, in its session, and the same user (token user SID);
otherwise set_hook fails with STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED. UIPI is checked first, as before.
Hooks in the hooker's own process, and on its own user's programs on the same desktop, are
unchanged; global hooks were already kept to the hooker's desktop.
---
--- a/server/hook.c
+++ b/server/hook.c
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
 #include "process.h"
 #include "request.h"
 #include "user.h"
+#include "security.h"
 
 struct hook_table;
 
@@ -422,6 +423,40 @@
 }
 
 /* set a window hook */
+/* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 8404): a hook on a thread of another process -- an in-context
+ * one (its module loads into that thread) or, since 8403, an out-of-context WinEvent hook
+ * (the events come back to the hooker) -- only on the hooker's own desktop, in its session,
+ * for its own user. Windows keeps hooks to one desktop; in a prefix several Unix users
+ * share, set_hook found the target by its thread id anywhere in the server, and one user
+ * could hook another's programs (a DLL in them, or their window events). Same-process
+ * hooks, and hooks on the user's own programs on the same desktop, are as before; UIPI
+ * (above) still decides for elevated targets. */
+static int sg_hook_target_allowed( struct desktop *desktop, struct thread *thread )
+{
+    struct desktop *target;
+    int same;
+
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_HOOK_ANY_SESSION
+    if (thread->process->session_id != current->process->session_id) return 0;
+#endif
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_HOOK_ANY_USER
+    if (!sg_token_same_user( current->process->token, thread->process->token )) return 0;
+#endif
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_HOOK_ANY_DESKTOP
+    if (!(target = get_thread_desktop( thread, 0 )))
+    {
+        clear_error();
+        return 0;
+    }
+    same = target == desktop;
+    release_object( target );
+    if (!same) return 0;
+#else
+    (void)target; (void)same;
+#endif
+    return 1;
+}
+
 DECL_HANDLER(set_hook)
 {
     struct process *process = NULL;
@@ -456,6 +491,13 @@
         {
             set_error( STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED );
             goto done;
+        }
+        /* and another process's thread only within the hooker's own desktop, session and
+         * user (8404) */
+        if (thread->process != current->process && !sg_hook_target_allowed( desktop, thread ))
+        {
+            set_error( STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED );
+            goto done;
         }
     }
 
